    "value": "No — Illinois's constitutional felony bar applies only to \"an office created by this Constitution\" (Illinois state and local offices) by its own text, not federal office; separately, the U.S. Constitution's own qualifications for Congress (age, citizenship, residency) can't be added to by any state, so this doesn't reach U.S. House or Senate candidates either way",
